.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-MACHINE-DECLINE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-machine-decline - Decline a machine a member asked to add to the team


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team machine decline <team> <machine-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Decline a machine a member asked to add to the team. Only owners and admins can.
--generation is optional: without it the command uses the team's current generation.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation (default: the current one)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for decline

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team machine decline acme m_abc123
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-machine(1)\fP
